Z||000000||pHoOl||02-25-2001||08:49 PM||||Around what mileage does the average Fiero V6 crap out?  A friend with a fiero just told me that they go around 120k, which would not be good considering i am only 100 miles away from it.  Also, if it does go, what is the cheapest way to get it back working again?  Rebuilding?  i've heard it's around 2500 to get it rebuilt.<P>thanks all<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who can't outrun the cops.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||02-25-2001||08:57 PM||||Depends on the care but 120k miles is considered way too soon. 180k-250k mile is more like it. Just listen for the timing chain rattling when it's cold. Sounds like rocks in the engine. When that starts, you better replace the chain right now.<P>I've had three engines beyond 200k. One blew the chain at 285k (I intentionally let it go. Bent the valves something serious), 265k (I rebuilt it and still used the original pistons), and my white SE is at 201k. <P>TK<P>Fuzz busters are for those who realize they can't outrun Motorola. <BR><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 02-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||pHoOl||02-25-2001||09:47 PM||||wow, okay, the kid said something about if you drive it hard it'll go out pretty quick around 120k.<P>Thanks for the help<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who can't outrun the cops.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||02-25-2001||10:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pHoOl:<BR><B>wow, okay, the kid said something about if you drive it hard it'll go out pretty quick around 120k.<P>Thanks for the help<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If it's been cared for, oil changed on a regular basis, and not been over-revved or just beat to hell, there's no reason to think that it's about to die. I've got an 88 4 cyl coupe with over 140K that sounds like a new engine. No knocks, taps, ticks, or other strange noises. Doesn't even use oil.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000004||Black88GT||02-25-2001||11:27 PM||||Just make sure you change the oil religiously.  Thats the main problem with the 2.8s, they have oiling problems which equal spun bearings, but if you maintain it right it should last you another 80k miles...||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||02-26-2001||01:05 AM||||My GT has 155,5xx miles on it, and I'm not really babying it, other than I try not to bring it above 5,500 and I let it warm up before I go above 3,000.  Burns some oil because the valve seals are shot and I know it's down on power, but if my oil pressure gauge is anywhere near right the pressure is still well within specs.  I still get a bit over 20mpg combined, and it starts up everytime.  I'm impressed! I thought I would have killed it by now...||||reg||1
Z||000006||fiero_hunter85||09-19-2001||02:59 PM||||iv seen alot of them that have over 200,000||||reg||1
